note: leaderboard — ordering records, and printing containers

a player has name as text, score as number, online as yesno

let players be an empty list of player
add (a player with name "ada", score 42, online yes) to players
add (a player with name "bob", score 91, online no) to players
add (a player with name "cara", score 42, online yes) to players

note: ascending and stable — ada stays ahead of cara on an equal score
say "by score:"
for each p in sorted players by score:
    say "  {p's name} {p's score}"

note: reverse the sorted copy for highest first
say "top first:"
for each p in reversed (sorted players by score):
    say "  {p's name} {p's score}"

note: a map always prints in sorted-key order, and yesno prints yes/no
let seen be a map from text to yesno
for each p in players:
    set item p's name of seen to p's online
say seen
